# tools/sanitizer/tsan.supp — the ThreadSanitizer lane's WORKING suppression
# list (task 1411). It is deliberately EMPTY, and that is a measured decision,
# not an unfinished file.
#
# WHY EMPTY
# ---------
# The one candidate phase 0 produced was `signal:thread_suspendHandler` — the
# druntime stop-the-world handler that TSan's deferred signal delivery
# deadlocks against. The lane does not need it: it runs under
# --DRT-gcopt=gc:manual, the world is never stopped, and that handler is never
# called. Adding a suppression to make the audit below non-vacuous would be
# exactly the defect this whole campaign exists to catch.
#
# WHAT AN ENTRY WOULD MEAN
# ------------------------
# A line here says: "TSan reports this, we have read it, it is not ours to fix,
# and here is who owns the decision." It is NOT the place to hide a real race —
# a suppressed race is not reported at all, so it cannot serve as evidence that
# the instrument is armed, and the lane's verdict function (tsan_expected.txt)
# is where a KNOWN race is declared instead. Suppress only what is not ours:
# druntime/Phobos/libc internals, or a third-party thread.
#
# FORMAT — every rule carries its own expiry evidence on the line ABOVE it:
#   # <YYYY-MM-DD> | <task> | <one reason>
#   <type>:<pattern>
# The metadata goes above and NOT after the rule: compiler-rt's suppression
# parser copies the rest of the line into the pattern, so a trailing `# ...`
# becomes part of the template and the rule then matches nothing — silently.
# Types are TSan's own: race, race_top, thread, mutex, signal, called_from_lib,
# deadlock. A rule without a task is not accepted at review.
#
# HOW A STALE LINE IS CAUGHT
# --------------------------
# `lane.d tsan-audit-suppressions` parses the `ThreadSanitizer: Matched N
# suppressions` block that print_suppressions=1 emits and FAILS on a declared
# line that matched zero times. Note the mechanic it has to allow for: at ZERO
# total matches the runtime prints NO BLOCK AT ALL — not "Matched 0" — so with
# a non-empty file, a missing block is a failure and not a zero.
#
# WHILE THIS FILE IS EMPTY THAT AUDIT IS VACUOUS, and it is not pretended
# otherwise. The witness for the whole mechanism is tsan_canary.supp, which is
# a SEPARATE file (so it suppresses nothing in the sweep) exercised twice every
# night by `lane.d tsan-selfcheck`: once without it (expect 1 report, no
# Matched block) and once with it (expect 0 reports and `Matched 1
# suppressions`). That one control proves symbolisation produces names, that
# matching is by name, and that the audit's parser sees the block.
